Yep. This is Document 3 — the implementation/rebuild document.

And I’m going to treat this differently from the old “Phase-by-Phase Replit Update Plan.” That old plan assumed the existing implementation was close enough to incrementally repair. V3 is a rebuild specification: the old repo is evidence/reference material, while the new documents define the intended product.

I’m also explicitly carrying forward what we just decided:

Rules are stable enough to implement, but not permanently frozen.

Ambiguous/undecided mechanics stay marked UNRESOLVED, with a temporary test rule where the engine needs deterministic behavior.

Hess AI is a first-class part of the game, not a feature to bolt on after the board works.

Existing played games are useful as behavioral evidence, but not as a sufficient test corpus.

Terminology can evolve; the implementation should avoid hard-coding awkward names everywhere.

This is Hess, not the old Royal Chess project. 😭



